      "side": 1,
      "message": "TL;DR looks like these call_depth_return_thunk__pkvm calls are correct: they are called not by vmx_pkvm_init() itself but by hypervisor functions called by it, when they return to vmx_pkvm_init(). (As you know, the host indeed calls some hypervisor functions, before deprivileging, using pkvm_sym().)\n\nSo the question: do we properly support this case (when the host calls hypervisor functions, i.e. functions that have different return thunks than the host)?\n\nDetails:\n\nOn bare metal (on ADL) I\u0027m not observing this problem either, but I\u0027m observing it in qemu VM. The call traces in debug vs non-debug mode are slightly different but similar:\n\nCONFIG_PKVM_INTEL_DEBUG\u003dy:\n\n```\n[    1.227850] Call Trace:\n[    1.227850]  \u003cTASK\u003e\n[    1.227850]  ? __die_body.cold+0x19/0x2c\n[    1.227850]  ? __die+0x2e/0x40\n[    1.227850]  ? page_fault_oops+0x154/0x2d0\n[    1.227850]  ? search_bpf_extables+0x64/0x90\n[    1.227850]  ? __pfx_memset__pkvm+0x7/0x10\n[    1.227850]  ? kernelmode_fixup_or_oops.isra.0+0x5f/0x70\n[    1.227850]  ? __bad_area_nosemaphore+0x161/0x1a0\n[    1.227850]  ? bad_area_nosemaphore+0x16/0x20\n[    1.227850]  ? do_kern_addr_fault+0x7b/0x90\n[    1.227850]  ? exc_page_fault+0x185/0x190\n[    1.227850]  ? asm_exc_page_fault+0x2b/0x30\n[    1.227850]  ? __pfx_memset__pkvm+0x7/0x10\n[    1.227850]  ? call_depth_return_thunk__pkvm+0x22/0x90\n[    1.227850]  ? pkvm_early_alloc_contig__pkvm+0x62/0x80\n[    1.227850]  vmx_pkvm_init+0x145/0xa70\n[    1.227850]  vmx_init+0x3e/0x160\n[    1.227850]  ? __pfx_vmx_init+0x10/0x10\n[    1.227850]  do_one_initcall+0x62/0x320\n[    1.227850]  kernel_init_freeable+0x245/0x2b0\n[    1.227850]  ? __pfx_kernel_init+0x10/0x10\n[    1.227850]  kernel_init+0x1e/0x150\n[    1.227850]  ret_from_fork+0x41/0x60\n[    1.227850]  ? __pfx_kernel_init+0x10/0x10\n[    1.227850]  ret_from_fork_asm+0x1a/0x30\n[    1.227850]  \u003c/TASK\u003e\n```\n\nCONFIG_PKVM_INTEL_DEBUG\u003dn:\n```\n[    1.238274] Call Trace:\n[    1.238274]  \u003cTASK\u003e\n[    1.238274]  ? __die_body.cold+0x19/0x2c\n[    1.238274]  ? __die+0x2e/0x40\n[    1.238274]  ? page_fault_oops+0x154/0x2d0\n[    1.238274]  ? search_bpf_extables+0x64/0x90\n[    1.238274]  ? call_depth_return_thunk__pkvm+0x4/0x90\n[    1.238274]  ? kernelmode_fixup_or_oops.isra.0+0x5f/0x70\n[    1.238274]  ? __bad_area_nosemaphore+0x161/0x1a0\n[    1.238274]  ? bad_area_nosemaphore+0x16/0x20\n[    1.238274]  ? do_kern_addr_fault+0x7b/0x90\n[    1.238274]  ? exc_page_fault+0x185/0x190\n[    1.238274]  ? asm_exc_page_fault+0x2b/0x30\n[    1.238274]  ? call_depth_return_thunk__pkvm+0x4/0x90\n[    1.238274]  ? vmx_pkvm_init+0x113/0x9f0\n[    1.238274]  vmx_init+0x3e/0x160\n[    1.238274]  ? __pfx_vmx_init+0x10/0x10\n[    1.238274]  do_one_initcall+0x62/0x320\n[    1.238274]  kernel_init_freeable+0x245/0x2b0\n[    1.238274]  ? __pfx_kernel_init+0x10/0x10\n[    1.238274]  kernel_init+0x1e/0x150\n[    1.238274]  ret_from_fork+0x41/0x60\n[    1.238274]  ? __pfx_kernel_init+0x10/0x10\n[    1.238274]  ret_from_fork_asm+0x1a/0x30\n[    1.238274]  \u003c/TASK\u003e\n```\n\nDisassembling the qemu VM at runtime via gdb shows that vmx_pkvm_init() itself calls call_depth_return_thunk, not call_depth_return_thunk__pkvm. But it only calls it at the end, which is much later than when the panic happens.\n\nFor the first call trace above (with CONFIG_PKVM_INTEL_DEBUG\u003dy), disassembly at vmx_pkvm_init+0x145:\n```\n   0xffffffff8352bcf0 \u003c+320\u003e:\tcall   0xffffffff82201a30 \u003cpkvm_early_alloc_contig\u003e\n   0xffffffff8352bcf5 \u003c+325\u003e:\tmov    %rax,0x8d50d4(%rip)        # 0xffffffff83e00dd0 \u003cpkvm_hyp__pkvm\u003e\n```\n\nAnd for the second call trace (with CONFIG_PKVM_INTEL_DEBUG\u003dn), disassembly at vmx_pkvm_init+0x113:\n```\n   0xffffffff8352acbe \u003c+270\u003e:\tcall   0xffffffff8220cf00 \u003cpkvm_per_cpu_nr_pages\u003e\n   0xffffffff8352acc3 \u003c+275\u003e:\tmov    -0xa62622(%rip),%rdi        # 0xffffffff82ac86a8 \u003cpage_offset_base\u003e\n```\n\nSo looks like the crash happens when vmx_pkvm_init() in the host calls hypervisor functions pkvm_early_alloc_contig() (in the first case) or pkvm_per_cpu_nr_pages() (in the second case), for example in pkvm_setup_pcpu():\n\n```\n\tnr_pages \u003d pkvm_sym(pkvm_per_cpu_nr_pages)();\n\tif (nr_pages) {\n\t\tvoid *per_cpu_base \u003d pkvm_sym(pkvm_early_alloc_contig)(nr_pages);\n```\n\nwhich then returns to vmx_pkvm_init() by calling call_depth_return_thunk__pkvm.",
